{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964699-ways-for-a-changeling-to-ward-off-ghosts","id":964699,"title":"Ways for a Changeling to ward off ghosts?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-06T18:44:17-07:00","id":964699,"title":"Ways for a Changeling to ward off ghosts?","content":"<b>Background</b>: I'm fairly new to the game, having just finished my second Changeling: The Lost session in my the first CoD campaign. Everyone in the group is a changeling, it is modern day in the US, there seems to be no shortage of vampire and werewolf npcs but the Storyteller tells us that supernaturals beyond changelings, vampires, and werewolves are exceedingly rare.<br /> <b>Problem</b>: We've encountered an NPC that has a haunting problem. Any time she stays in a place for longer than 10 hours, ghosts tend to show up, and so she's been forced to constantly stay on the move for many years. My character really wants to help her, if possible. My question is, are there any contracts, merits, or anything that a changeling could gain access to that would keep ghosts away? Closest I've found was a contract that let me speak with ghosts, but we already have someone in the party who can do that and being able to talk to these ghosts does no good.<br /> The storyteller seems pretty flexible in what books he allows. We're playing in 2.5e but he allows content from older books with his approval.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12390-gadren","name":"gadren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T19:47:30-07:00","id":964731,"title":"","content":"You could always make a Goblin Vow with Ghosts, or maybe Hauntings to be more specific. There's also the option of entering her dreams to look for any clues about what's causing the haunting and working from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T20:05:45-07:00","id":964737,"title":"","content":"You could go drastic and take Phantom Glory to just start punching them? That's all I can suggest. But really, I think some Occult investigation is your best bet, to find the source of the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T20:12:52-07:00","id":964739,"title":"","content":"Do any of the Motley have the Gravewright Kith, or do any in the Freehold have it? While it's only a temporary solution, they can always use their Kith Blessing to remove the Anchor Condition when ghosts start showing up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T20:15:40-07:00","id":964740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964699-ways-for-a-changeling-to-ward-off-ghosts?p=964739#post964739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do any of the Motley have the Gravewright Kith, or do any in the Freehold have it? While it's only a temporary solution, they can always use their Kith Blessing to remove the Anchor Condition when ghosts start showing up.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if no one has it, look for someone with Riddle-Kith. Next best thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vect